# ── Experiment outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated files are ignored by default so the repo stays clean and you
# never accidentally commit a half-finished run.
#
# BUT: once you have a FINAL run you're reporting in your paper, commit it
# on purpose so the numbers in the paper are traceable to the data that
# produced them:
#
#     git add -f python/results/metrics.csv python/results/predictions_*.csv
#
# Note the full path. A pattern with a slash inside it is anchored to the
# repository root, so a bare `results/*` would NOT match python/results/ one
# level down. `git check-ignore -v <path>` tells you which rule actually fired.
python/results/*
!python/results/.gitkeep

# Your working notes, if you keep them in the repo
notes/
*.local.md
